# Plan: customer satisfaction rating

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12). Written 2026-10-07. Nothing is built yet.
Test command: `node --test` (the stack profile reports `npm` missing on this machine; `package.json` maps `npm test` to the same command).

## Goal

A customer rates a resolved ticket 1 to 5 from the portal, once. A 1 or 2 emails the owner. A nightly job writes a
seven-day summary per agent. `assignee_id` becomes `owner_id`.

## Read this first

The answers to the questions I would have asked you are in [decisions.md](decisions.md), each with the answer I
recommend. The phases are written on those answers. Three of them change what you might expect from the spec:

- **D1.** Requirement 6 says "everywhere". `src/jobs/export-tickets.js` dumps tickets as stored into
  `exports/tickets.json`, which finance's reporting job reads and deploys on its own schedule. Renaming the field
  there would break their job without warning. The plan renames it everywhere in this repo and keeps an
  `assignee_id` copy in the export file until finance confirms they have switched.
- **D2.** Production runs on Postgres and that adapter is not in this repo. The column rename, the two new rating
  columns, the summary table and the nightly runner entry are not done by this plan. Phase 1 and 2 write them out as
  hand-over notes.
- **D3.** A closed ticket cannot be rated (the glossary says closed is final). The customer has the three quiet days
  after resolving.

## Phases

| # | Phase | Class | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Rename `assignee_id` to `owner_id`](phase-01-rename-owner.md) | COUNCIL (touches an external contract and a schema); proceed on D1 and D2 | not started |
| 2 | [Store and accept a rating](phase-02-rating-storage.md) | ACT, tenant scoping is a hot path | not started |
| 3 | [Email the owner on a low score](phase-03-low-score-email.md) | ACT | not started |
| 4 | [Weekly summary job](phase-04-weekly-summary.md) | ACT | not started |
| 5 | [Review, docs, hand-over](phase-05-review-and-handover.md) | ACT, includes the independent review | not started |

Order matters: phase 1 first so the new code never uses the old name; phase 3 and 4 both need phase 2.

## Files

- Modify: `src/tickets.js`, `src/portal.js`, `src/store.js`, `src/jobs/export-tickets.js`, `docs/glossary.md`,
  `README.md`, `test/tickets.test.js`, `test/export-tickets.test.js`.
- Create: `src/jobs/weekly-rating-summary.js`, `test/rating.test.js`, `test/weekly-rating-summary.test.js`.

## Execution

Inline, in one session, stopping after phase 1 (D1/D2 sign-off) and after phase 5's review. Subagent-driven is not
worth it for roughly 150 lines of code. Each phase ends in its own commit; nothing is pushed.

## Hot paths

Phase 2 enforces the organisation check on a customer-facing call (tenant scoping). Phase 5 has an independent
review by someone other than the author, with a negative control on the isolation test.

## Not in this plan

Free-text comments on a rating, changing a rating, a customer-facing "thank you" mail, team-lead dashboards,
renaming the `assignTicket` function. None are in the spec.
